  <revision rev="8" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>8aab89a6e56dd44696ac29d4e8a774f6</srcmd5>
    <version>6.4.0</version>
    <time>1787939243</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update to RE/flex 6.4.0.

Upstream: improved DFA growth control (the edge count and the accumulated
positions are now capped alongside the state count, and the state cap itself
is tightened to a third of the previous limit, so pathological patterns fail
with exceeds_limits instead of growing unbounded), AbstractMatcher::set_end()
defaults to true, and a large CMake build overhaul.

Heads-up - this is a real soname bump: libreflex.so.6 -&gt; libreflex.so.6.4,
so libreflex6 is renamed to libreflex6_4. reflex::Pattern grew by 16 bytes in
6.4.0 (34784 -&gt; 34800 bytes, measured across the 6.0.0-6.4.0 headers), and the
reflex generator emits &quot;static const reflex::Pattern PATTERN_&lt;cond&gt;(...)&quot; into
every generated scanner, so the object size is baked into consumers. Upstream
declares no ABI stability between releases (its CMake package version file is
ExactVersion), so the soversion now tracks major.minor. No Obsoletes: old and
new library packages are co-installable while consumers are rebuilt.

The only reverse dependency in Factory is falcosecurity-container-plugin,
which reaches re-flex through re-flex-devel (name unchanged), so it needs a
rebuild but no source change and no coupled submission. Expect a somewhat
longer staging dwell than a plain version bump.

Other packaging changes:
- new libreflexmin6_4 subpackage: upstream's CMake build now also builds the
  minimal runtime library; -devel ships both pkg-config files.
- %check now runs upstream's rtest regression suite (registered via CTest
  in 6.4.0).
- dropped the x86-64-v3 BuildConstraint (boo#1246164): 6.4.0 probes SIMD
  support by compiling instead of running and applies the AVX2/AVX512BW
  flags only to the sources that need them, so the build result no longer
  depends on the build host's CPU and the baseline code stays SSE2.
- reflex-shared-soversion.patch rebased onto the reworked CMakeLists.txt; it
  now derives the soversion from the project version instead of hardcoding it.</comment>
    <requestid>1374117</requestid>
  </revision>
